  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SRK - Cruz Vermelha - Mocambique</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SRK - Cruz Vermelha - Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mo&#xE7;ambique &#xE4;r ett land med h&#xF6;g s&#xE5;rbarhet och l&#xE5;g motst&#xE5;ndskraft mot naturrelaterade katastrofer. P&#xE5; olika utvecklingsindex hamnar landet l&#xE5;ngt ned och fattigdomen &#xE4;r utbredd. Tillg&#xE5;ngen till adekvata vatten- och sanitetssystem &#xE4;r l&#xE5;g, och risken f&#xF6;r sjukdomar s&#xE5; som malaria eller vattenburna &#xE5;kommor &#xE4;r h&#xF6;g. F&#xF6;r att adressera n&#xE5;gra av de utmaningar Mo&#xE7;ambiques befolkning tampas med beh&#xF6;vs insatser f&#xF6;r att minska samh&#xE4;llens och individers s&#xE5;rbarhet, inte minst inf&#xF6;r externa shocker och kriser som kopplar till klimatf&#xF6;r&#xE4;ndringar. 

F&#xF6;r att svara upp mot utmaningar som kopplar till s&#xE5; v&#xE4;l samh&#xE4;llens l&#xE5;ga kapacitet att hantera effekter av naturrelaterade kriser, som bristande tillg&#xE5;ng till rent vatten och fullgoda sanitetsstrukturer samt f&#xE5; alternativ till f&#xF6;rs&#xF6;rjningm&#xF6;jligheter f&#xF6;resl&#xE5;r svenska ambassaden i Mo&#xE7;ambique att bist&#xE5; med finansiering till det svenska R&#xF6;da Korset (SRK) och den mo&#xE7;ambikanska nationella f&#xF6;reningen Cruz Vermelha Mo&#xE7;ambique f&#xF6;r att minska risker och s&#xE5;rbarheter i Mo&#xE7;ambiques Manicaprovins. Projeket som &#xE4;r aktuellt f&#xF6;r finansiering &#xE4;r PREPA-projektet (Project for Resilience and Enhanced Preparedness and Action), vilket &#xE4;r ett fyra&#xE5;rigt projekt med en budget p&#xE5; 57 392 199 SEK. 

Insatsen kommer inkludera aktiviteter som fokuserar p&#xE5; katastrofriskreducering, klimatanpassning, h&#xE5;llbara f&#xF6;rs&#xF6;rjningsm&#xF6;jligheter, h&#xE4;lsa, samt vatten och sanitet, och ta avstamp i de lokala samh&#xE4;llenas identiferade behov. Med syfte att fr&#xE4;mja l&#xE5;ngsiktighet kommer en central komponent av projektet utg&#xF6;ra kapacitetsst&#xE4;rkande av CVM som en viktig nationell akt&#xF6;r. Vidare kommer en s k crisis modifyer (CM) att utarbetas under projektets g&#xE5;ng, vilken kommer att ge SRK och CVM m&#xF6;jlighet att svara upp mot kontextuella f&#xF6;r&#xE4;ndring i projektets upptagningomr&#xE5;de (eller dess omedelbara n&#xE4;rhet), och p&#xE5; s&#xE5; vis reducera risken av eskalerande humanit&#xE4;ra behov. CM mekanismen kommer utformas p&#xE5; ett s&#xE5;dant s&#xE4;tt att den fortsatt kan vara i bruk efter projektets avslut, och d&#xE4;rmed st&#xE4;rka den nationella responskapaciteten.

Projektet kommer att f&#xF6;rl&#xE4;ggas till 15 olika samh&#xE4;llen i spridda &#xF6;ver de tre distrikten Machaze, Mussorize och Sussundenga. Kvinnor, flickor, m&#xE4;n och pojkar i de samh&#xE4;llen som anses mest s&#xE5;rbara f&#xF6;r h&#xE4;lso- , klimat- och naturkatastrofrelaterade risker kommer att prioriteras. Arbetsmetoden kommer bygga p&#xE5; m&#xE5;lgruppens deltagande och inkludering i planering och utf&#xF6;rande av aktiviteter.  Avtalspart &#xE4;r SRK, vilka ocks&#xE5; kommer att bist&#xE5; med teknisk kunskap och st&#xF6;d, samt tr&#xE4;ning och uppf&#xF6;ljning, medan utf&#xF6;rande part &#xE4;r CVM. Tv&#xE5; till tre SRK-delegater kommer att vara stationerade i Mo&#xE7;ambique under projektets g&#xE5;ng.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To respond to challenges related to communities low coping capacities to natural hazards, poor access to water and sanitation, and lack of livelihood opportunities in Mozambique&apos;s Manica Province, the Embassy if Sweden (EoS) is proposing to fund the Swedish Red Cross (SRC) and the Mozambiqan national society Cruz Vermelha Mo&#xE7;ambique (CVM) with 57 392 199 SEK over a four year period. The project, Project for Resilience and Enhanced Preparedness and Action (PREPA), has the purpose of reducing risk and vulnerability to crisis considering the impact of climate change and environmental degradation. It will be a community-based intervention which includes disaster risk reduction, climate change adaptation, sustainable livelihoods as well as health and WASH. In order to apply a sustainable approach, a key component of the project will also be to develop and enhance the institutional capacity of CVM as a key national and local actor.

A crisis modifier (CM) will be established, which will give SRC and CVM the possibility to respond in accordance with contextual changes in the project&apos;s intervention area (or immediate proximity). It&apos;s purpose is to reduce the risk of escalating humanitarian needs. The intention is that the CM mechanism will remain in use also after the completion of this project, and as such contribute to a strengthened national response capacity. 

The project will take place in 15 communities across three districts; Machaze, Mussorize and Sussundenga. Focus will be placed on women, girls, men and boys in communities most vulnerable to health risks, climate change risks and natural hazards. A participatory approach will be applied, placing focus on a community led intervention. The project will be implemented by CVM, with the support of SRC who will provide technical support, training and monitoring. Two to three delegates will be present in country across the project period.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to strengthen the resilience of women and men of all ages and backgrounds, including those living with various disabilities, in targeted high-risk vulnerable communities in Manica province through improved livelihood opportunities, reduction of disaster risk as well as adaptation to climate change and climate/environment-related health challenges. This overall objective is underpinned by four outcomes, whereof which three are operational, and one of enabling nature;

Outcome 1) Disaster risks/natural hazards: Increased capacity of women, men, girls and boys in the target communities to cope with, mitigate, prepare for, and respond to climate change and natural hazards (floods, cyclones and drought).

Outcome 2) Livelihoods: Women, men, girls and boys in the target communities have improved or diversified livelihood opportunities through climate-resilient and environmentally sustainable livelihoods programming.

Outcome 3) Health: Women, men, girls and boys most at risk in the target communities have improved health status.

Outcome 4) Response and resilience programming capacities: CVM governance, staff and volunteers have the technical capacities to respond to emerging disasters and support community resilience.

The project will target approximately 3000 households amounting to 15 000 people (approximately 51 % women and 49 % men) in 15 different communities which will be identified at the beginning of the project;  400 selected staff from CVM (HQ, province delegation in Manica and selected districts&apos; delegations) including volunteers in the target communities (45 % women and 55 % men) and; communities in provinces eligible for the Simplified Early Action Protocol on Cholera (S-EAP-C) and Crisis Modifier Fund (CMF).</narrative>
  </description>
